My python DT_DYNAMIC parser is buggy (the mapping of vaddr to offset — PT_DYNAMIC's p_vaddr vs p_offset; I used p_offset for reading but then v2o for the string table; but the issue is my `loads` for PT_LOAD: p_vaddr, p_filesz; and I need p_memsz. Also I read d.index for null terminator but the string offset may point to garbage). Anyway, the `--list` output from the loader is authoritative and it works:

**libmain.nv.so** needs: libc.so, libm.so, libstdc++.so, /system/bin/linker (interp), libgcc_s.so.1
**libunity.nv.so** needs: libmain.so, libc.so, libm.so, libGLESv2.so, libstdc++.so, libz.so, /system/bin/linker, libdl.so.2, libpthread.so.0, librt.so.1, libdrm.so.2, libgcc_s.so.1
**libil2cpp.nv.so** needs: liblog.so, libstdc++.so, libm.so, /lib/ld-linux-armhf.so.3, libgcc_s.so.1

Note: `/system/bin/linker` as interp — the patch_interp.py presumably patches the PT_INTERP to /lib/ld-linux-armhf.so.3.

So the important SONAMEs to map in dep3:
- libc.so → /lib/arm-linux-gnueabihf/libc.so.6  ✓
- libm.so → /lib/arm-linux-gnueabihf/libm.so.6 ✓
- libstdc++.so → /usr/lib/arm-linux-gnueabihf/libstdc++.so.6 ✓
- libz.so → /usr/lib/arm-linux-gnueabihf/libz.so.1.3.1 ✓
- libGLESv2.so → /usr/lib/arm-linux-gnueabihf/libGLESv2.so (libMali) ✓
- libmain.so → hf/libmain.nv.so ✓
