Hmm, wait. Actually there IS a subtlety: GCC may optimize `pthread_cond_wait(c,m)` call within the same TU to a direct call... no, it can't, because the function is not `static` and has default visibility; with -fPIC it must go through PLT (unless -fno-semantic-interposition isn't the default... actually GCC's default IS to assume semantic interposition, so it calls through PLT). Either way, the PLT resolves to our own definition (first in scope). ✓

Now — **the big question: does the interposition actually take effect for the game libraries?**

The game libs (libunity.so, libil2cpp.so) are dlopened by hs-loader with RTLD_NOW|RTLD_GLOBAL. Their undefined symbols are resolved at dlopen time using the global scope: the executable + its DT_NEEDED + previously dlopen'd RTLD_GLOBAL libs. If `libbioniccompat.so` is a DT_NEEDED of hs-loader, it's in the global scope at position right after hs-loader and before libc. ✓

